    year: 628,
    description: "Having lost Egypt, Syria, Palestine, and Anatolia to Persia, Heraclius launches a campaign of staggering audacity: instead of defending what remains, he strikes through the Caucasus deep into the Persian heartland (622–628 AD), devastating the sacred fire-temples of Zoroastrianism. In 626, while he is deep in enemy territory, Avars and Persians simultaneously besiege Constantinople - and fail, the city held by the Patriarch and the city walls while Heraclius fights 1,000 miles away. In 628 the Persian king Khosrow II is overthrown and murdered by his own son Kavad II, who immediately sues for peace. All Byzantine territory is restored; the True Cross is returned; Heraclius enters Constantinople in triumph. It is the greatest military comeback in Byzantine history. Four years later the first Arab raids into Byzantine Syria begin. Everything won is lost again within a decade.",
