    title: 'Bulgarian Second Empire Founded',
    year: 1185,
    description: "Brothers Peter and Asen - Bulgarian nobles - travel to Constantinople to petition Emperor Andronikos I for a grant of land in recognition of their military service. He refuses them contemptuously. They return home to Tarnovo and raise a revolt, invoking Saint Demetrius (patron of Thessalonica) who they claim has abandoned the Greeks to the Normans and now favours the Bulgarians. The timing is perfect: Andronikos is collapsing, the Normans are ravaging Greece, and Byzantine military resources are exhausted. By 1186 the rebellion has become the Second Bulgarian Empire, with Tarnovo as its capital. The empire defeats Byzantine forces at the Battle of Lardea (1190), and Emperor Isaac II is forced to recognise Bulgarian independence. The Second Bulgarian Empire will last until 1396, and its founding represents the permanent end of Byzantine control over the northern Balkans.",
