    description: "In July 1261, the Nicaean general Alexios Strategopoulos discovers that the Latin garrison of Constantinople has sailed away to raid a Nicaean-allied island, leaving the city barely defended. He scales the walls at night with a small force and opens the gates. The Latin Emperor Baldwin II flees barefoot through the streets and escapes by boat, carrying the Crown of Thorns and leaving behind his imperial seal. Michael VIII Palaiologos enters Constantinople barefoot in religious procession behind an icon of the Virgin, who he credits with the reconquest. He is crowned again in the Hagia Sophia. The Latin Empire has lasted 57 years. But the Constantinople Michael recovers is a shadow of what the Crusaders sacked: the population is a fraction of what it was, the palaces are derelict, the Venetians and Genoese control the trade of the Aegean, and the territorial empire barely extends beyond the city walls on the European side.",
