    description: "Sultan Murad I captures Adrianople (the ancient city of Hadrianopolis, now Edirne) around 1369 and moves the Ottoman capital there from Bursa in Anatolia - a statement of intent that the Ottoman future lies in Europe, not Asia. Adrianople is 220 kilometres from Constantinople on the European side; with the Asian shore already firmly in Ottoman hands, Constantinople is now completely surrounded by Ottoman territory. The city holds out only because the Ottomans find a subservient Byzantine emperor - paying tribute, providing troops for Ottoman campaigns, watching in vassalage - more immediately useful than the rubble of a stormed city. Byzantine territory has been reduced to Constantinople itself, a sliver of the Black Sea coast, and the Despotate of Morea in the Peloponnese. The empire that once stretched from Spain to Syria now consists of a single walled city and its suburbs.",
