    description: "On June 28, 1389 - the feast of Saint Vitus - the Ottoman Sultan Murad I meets a Serbian-Bosnian coalition under Prince Lazar Hrebeljanovic on the Kosovo plain. Both commanders die: Murad is killed during or after the battle, possibly by the Serbian knight Milos Obilic in a feigned submission; Lazar is captured and executed. The battle is tactically inconclusive but strategically decisive: Serbia becomes an Ottoman vassal state. For Byzantium, Kosovo removes the last significant Christian buffer state between Constantinople and the full weight of Ottoman power. The city is now an island of Christianity in an Ottoman sea, kept alive only because the Ottomans find a vassal Byzantine emperor more useful than rubble. Bayezid I tightens the blockade of Constantinople immediately after Kosovo; the city's fall is now a matter of when, not whether.",
