    description: "On the night of September 3, 1843, military officers and Athenian civilians surround the royal palace and demand a constitution. Otto, the Bavarian-born Catholic king of a Greek Orthodox nation, finds himself completely without support: his Bavarian guard has been sent home, and no Greek rallies to defend royal absolutism. He capitulates before dawn. Greece's first constitution establishes a bicameral parliament, guarantees civil liberties, and ends the decade of Bavarian regency rule. The event is described by contemporaries as a 'revolution without blood,' though the power behind it is military. Otto remains king but his authority is permanently curtailed. The constitution does not solve the deep problems of Greek governance - a weak state, factionalised politics, and British-French-Russian interference in every election - but it establishes the parliamentary form within which those struggles will be fought for generations.",
